    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Question\n\nHello!\r\n\r\nWhen using `saiw\"` to add double-quotes, the cursor is moved to the start of the word, as show below: \r\n\r\n![output](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/276d779a-7121-40b0-a524-45bb15c25670)\r\n\r\nFrom my understanding, this is the default behavior of the `iw` motion.\r\n\r\nI would prefer that the cursor stays at the same position, regardless of the motion. I don't understand how to approach this problem - should I use markers, should I save the cursor position before `Minisurround.add()`, or...?\r\n\r\nAny guidance would be appreciated!",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.surround</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When using <code class=\"notranslate\">saiw\"</code> to add double-quotes, the cursor is moved to the start of the word, as show below:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/102469559/497626277-276d779a-7121-40b0-a524-45bb15c25670.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTI5MDYsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MjYwNiwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMDI0Njk1NTkvNDk3NjI2Mjc3LTI3NmQ3NzlhLTcxMjEtNDBiMC1hNTI0LTQ1YmIxNWMyNTY3MC5naWY_.-gPwYQZp1NrodqBvQieL4BCD5x2wqXacODetmKgeh1Y\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/102469559/497626277-276d779a-7121-40b0-a524-45bb15c25670.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTI5MDYsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MjYwNiwicGF0aCI6Ii8xMDI0Njk1NTkvNDk3NjI2Mjc3LTI3NmQ3NzlhLTcxMjEtNDBiMC1hNTI0LTQ1YmIxNWMyNTY3MC5naWY_.-gPwYQZp1NrodqBvQieL4BCD5x2wqXacODetmKgeh1Y\" alt=\"output\" data-animated-image=\"\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">From my understanding, this is the default behavior of the <code class=\"notranslate\">iw</code> motion.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I would prefer that the cursor stays at the same position, regardless of the motion. I don't understand how to approach this problem - should I use markers, should I save the cursor position before <code class=\"notranslate\">Minisurround.add()</code>, or...?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any guidance would be appreciated!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.surround\nQuestion\nHello!\nWhen using saiw\" to add double-quotes, the cursor is moved to the start of the word, as show below:\n\nFrom my understanding, this is the default behavior of the iw motion.\nI would prefer that the cursor stays at the same position, regardless of the motion. I don't understand how to approach this problem - should I use markers, should I save the cursor position before Minisurround.add(), or...?\nAny guidance would be appreciated!",
